- **src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx** (`getStaticProps`): This is the main catch-all page data fetcher (confirmed at line 66) that orchestrates all Contentstack SDK calls (getSingletonEntry, getSingleEntry, getHeaderAndFooter, etc.) and passes the resulting content as props to ContentstackProvider. Live Preview requires detecting preview mode (via query params/cookies) and fetching draft content from Contentstack instead of published content. Currently getStaticProps only fetches published entries — it has no preview-mode branch, so CMS editors never see draft/unpublished content in the live preview iframe.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add preview-mode detection at the top of getStaticProps: check context.preview and/or context.previewData for Contentstack live-preview parameters (preview token, content_type_uid, entry_uid). When preview mode is active, pass those parameters through to the Contentstack SDK calls (getSingletonEntry/getSingleEntry) so they query the preview/draft content delivery endpoint instead of the published one. This requires the Contentstack SDK initialization (wherever Stack is instantiated) to also accept live_preview config — but the gatekeeper is getStaticProps, which must read context.preview and route it into the fetch calls.


